<body>
<h1>Grad-Shafranov Equilibrium Equation (Solov'ev Linear Source Model)</h1>

<h2>General strong form</h2>
<p>The poloidal flux $\psi(R,Z)$ in cylindrical coordinates $(R,Z)$ satisfies the
elliptic Grad-Shafranov equation, where $\Delta^{*}$ is the Grad-Shafranov operator:</p>
<p>
$$
\Delta^{*}\psi \;\equiv\; R\,\frac{\partial}{\partial R}\!\left(\frac{1}{R}\,\frac{\partial \psi}{\partial R}\right)
+ \frac{\partial^{2}\psi}{\partial Z^{2}}
\;=\; -\,\mu_{0}\,R^{2}\,\frac{dp}{d\psi} \;-\; F\,\frac{dF}{d\psi}.
$$
</p>

<h2>Solov'ev linear source model (strong form)</h2>
<p>Choosing the Solov'ev closure with $\mu_{0}\,dp/d\psi = C_{1}$ and $F\,dF/d\psi = C_{2}$
makes the right-hand side a simple linear source, yielding a linear elliptic problem:</p>
<p>
$$
R\,\frac{\partial}{\partial R}\!\left(\frac{1}{R}\,\frac{\partial \psi}{\partial R}\right)
+ \frac{\partial^{2}\psi}{\partial Z^{2}}
\;=\; -\left(C_{1}\,R^{2} + C_{2}\right)
\qquad \text{in } \Omega \subset \{(R,Z)\}.
$$
</p>

<h2>Boundary conditions</h2>
<p>Homogeneous Dirichlet condition on the plasma boundary $\partial\Omega$:</p>
<p>
$$
\psi = 0 \qquad \text{on } \partial\Omega.
$$
</p>

<h2>Weak (variational) form</h2>
<p>Dividing by $R$ uses the identity
$\tfrac{1}{R}\Delta^{*}\psi = \nabla\!\cdot\!\big(\tfrac{1}{R}\nabla\psi\big)$,
where $\nabla=(\partial_R,\partial_Z)$. Multiplying by a test function
$v \in H_{0}^{1}(\Omega)$, integrating over $\Omega$, and integrating by parts
(the boundary term vanishes since $v=0$ on $\partial\Omega$):</p>
<p>
Find $\psi \in H_{0}^{1}(\Omega)$ such that for all $v \in H_{0}^{1}(\Omega)$:
$$
\int_{\Omega} \frac{1}{R}\,\nabla\psi \cdot \nabla v \; dR\,dZ
\;=\;
\int_{\Omega} \left(C_{1}\,R + \frac{C_{2}}{R}\right) v \; dR\,dZ.
$$
</p>

<p>Bilinear and linear forms:</p>
<p>
$$
a(\psi,v) = \int_{\Omega} \frac{1}{R}\,\nabla\psi \cdot \nabla v \; dR\,dZ,
\qquad
L(v) = \int_{\Omega} \left(C_{1}\,R + \frac{C_{2}}{R}\right) v \; dR\,dZ.
$$
</p>
</body>
</html>
